<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>IIHF ordered to allow Russia back into world championships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2501525325c580e4f86855f8a089272531052ad51e1ba337cbff2b44224e18f9</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iihf-ordered-to-allow-russia-back-into-world-championships/a-79805650--8e19bd1daa6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iihf-ordered-to-allow-russia-back-into-world-championships/a-79805650?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Court of Arbitration for Sport has ruled that Russian teams must be allowed to take part in international ice hockey tournaments. The IIHF had banned Russia following the country's full-scale invasion of Ukraine.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Franz Reindl elected new IIHF president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19c194e0d963f0cfb5169e2635bb3a07c86652884a9ab6b52197a433b9dae9cf</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-franz-reindl-elected-new-iihf-president/a-79521799--24f017ae08ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-franz-reindl-elected-new-iihf-president/a-79521799?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Franz Reindl has been elected president of ice hockey's world governing body. The former forward was a member of West Germany's Olympic bronze medal-winning team.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Alexander Ovechkin backs Putin party in campaign video</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4af5867e016c652ec522fc850a60f9374eac5174463573954c932ca19e349e1b</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772--a8049deceb76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey legend Alexander Ovechkin has lent Vladimir Putin's party a helping hand in its parliamentary election campaign. That's in keeping with a pattern of support by an athlete who claims not to be political.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Austria women ice hockey team fight for future generations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08296a90f4840d34dadbbbce75c3503a0913ae6dc39f76a6da46260a25ef8420</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578--abef88f6b631.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Austria are getting ready for their first Women's Ice Hockey World Championship. But preparations have been overshadowed by a dispute about conditions, pay and getting men's cast-off kit. A solution now looks in sight.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Alexander Zverev clinches tennis No. 1 ranking</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7626ed647fd5b925dc0d456b0f1940afc7c2e0612f64acfa7fd617efbc998610</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T22:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alexander-zverev-clinches-tennis-no-1-ranking/a-79803048--1b03a09b61b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alexander-zverev-clinches-tennis-no-1-ranking/a-79803048?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev is the second German man, after Boris Becker, to clinch the No. 1 spot in tennis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich's Kenya friendly highlights Africa's growing pull for global sport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80230c39b40ff0e9dcf2d1b9beb992f27a5784c2028bf99dcd5b88e8a9befc67</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753--c6f4b50cf1c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich are to open Nairobi's new Raila Odinga International Stadium against Ajax as Kenya prepares for AFCON 2027. The match highlights Africa's growing sports ambitions — and questions over cost and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich head coach Vincent Kompany's health scare highlights the need for better support for elite coaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1707c345dab6b759eb06bdace4c8ffb0b4571b93b57dbf312c03b1d2f1d09408</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-e/a-79764661--fcbaed2aac2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-elite-coaches/a-79764661?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Vincent Kompany’s health concern is a reminder that elite football's pressures affect coaches too. Better support, clearer structures and mental health safeguards are increasingly vital.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's first Youth Olympics open in Senegal amid hope and scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb7c63eb3de4a7091a82ee1f82d2f8728f978ed47f97dbbc59c0ac209c2bdf29</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478--c3155dbcff43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senegal is hosting Africa's first Youth Olympics, with 2,700 young athletes competing in Dakar, Diamniadio and Saly. The Games bring pride and hope, but also questions over cost, rights and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Kane: Ballon d’Or for Bayern Munich striker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc41635e1a6e488a8b1e55a25711648da8e210a6987277d86fa6c1fcc34feb4b</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299--2a5c9f9ed870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane has won football's most prestigious individual prize, beating Kylian Mbappe and Lamine Yamal. Kane has developed even more in the Bundesliga despite an uneven league.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany sit out FIFA Under-15 World Cup as Russia return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:047be767f60a93322ba7897fcf428129963e02b485dffcf5a7913a28e5a57363</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T07:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-sit-out-fifa-under-15-world-cup-as-russia-return/a-79734040--d1c93bdcd718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-sit-out-fifa-under-15-world-cup-as-russia-return/a-79734040?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany is one a handful of FIFA's 211 nations to refuse an invitation to play at the inaugural Under-15 World Cup. The tournament will also mark Russia's return to the FIFA fold.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester City, the UAE and the UK's OM in a political tangle</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dfad5e34ba41d6e991522a8797c994285a5b7ed905808f4e2437ca985b22256</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-the-uae-and-the-uk-s-om-in-a-political-tangle/a-79664729--11ae1f17a0ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-the-uae-and-the-uk-s-om-in-a-political-tangle/a-79664729?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nearly 20 years after arriving in England, Manchester City's UAE owners could exit amid cheating charges. That would pose a challenge for a city — and prime minister — closely tied to Abu Dhabi.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>FIFPRO report highlights growing pains in women's football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8002135decd4c7b4f8d25697f55d99b0031310967d83abd5050d2e411b6f21a5</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T08:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifpro-report-highlights-growing-pains-in-women-s-football/a-79648013--365fa34aee7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifpro-report-highlights-growing-pains-in-women-s-football/a-79648013?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Expected global revenue of over $1 billion and new faces at the U17 World Cup show women's football is booming, but a recent report also highlights need for better structures globally.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>World Cup 2034: Does Saudi Arabia shelving Neom Stadium spell trouble?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fb167618da8f90391088dfb2ee3fc5d1ced141b663db7dacf6f201d697a7aa3</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948--b8b608a266b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since winning the right to hold the 2034 World Cup unopposed, Saudi Arabia has been pulling away from sport. With reports that its most ambitious stadium project will be abandoned, what does this mean for the World Cup?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
